# Line endings
#
# `graphcal format` emits LF unconditionally — a canonical formatter has one
# canonical output, and line endings are part of it. A CRLF working copy
# therefore reports every source file as unformatted and would be rewritten
# wholesale on the next `graphcal format` run.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a
# Windows checkout converts every tracked text file to CRLF. Pin the working
# tree to LF on all platforms rather than relying on each contributor's local
# Git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be line-ending converted. `text=auto` already
# applies Git's binary heuristic, but state the known types explicitly so a
# misdetected fixture cannot be silently corrupted.
*.png binary
*.bin binary
*.wasm binary
